From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: goodix - don't fail suspend when screen-off is NACKed

Some GT911 boards NACK the screen-off command after INT is pulled low,
which aborts system suspend. Carry on instead: resume already resets and
reconfigures the controller when it doesn't answer.

---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
@@ -1499,9 +1499,9 @@
 	error = goodix_i2c_write_u8(ts->client, GOODIX_REG_COMMAND,
 				    GOODIX_CMD_SCREEN_OFF);
 	if (error) {
-		goodix_irq_direction_input(ts);
-		goodix_request_irq(ts);
-		return -EAGAIN;
+		/* Some boards NACK screen-off; resume resets the controller when it doesn't answer */
+		dev_warn(dev, "screen-off failed: %d\n", error);
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	/*
